TI  - Tunneled pleural catheter dysfunction: case report and review of complications.
PG  - 149-52
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3182537d05 [doi]
AB  - Tunneled pleural catheters (TPC) are often used for management of malignant 
      pleural effusion. They have proven to be safe, effective, and are associated with 
      low rates of complications. We describe the case of a patient with metastatic 
      renal cell carcinoma who inadvertently cut his TPC causing leakage of pleural 
      fluid, requiring urgent removal. We review the reported complications of TPC in 
      the literature and suggest close vigilance of patients at risk to have altered 
      mental status who undergo placement of TPC.
