AB  - Malignant pleural effusion (MPE) is a known complication of both thoracic and 
      extra thoracic malignancies. The presence of MPE regardless of the primary site 
      translates into advanced stage disease. Diagnosis and management of MPE with the 
      goals of palliation and improving quality of life poses a challenge for chest 
      physicians. Recently, multiple studies have made attempts to answer questions 
      regarding optimal management in various clinical scenarios. We will review the 
      current evidence and available options for the management of MPE.
