TI  - Hemothorax treated with indwelling tunneled pleural catheter: are all 
      hemothoraces the same?
PG  - 261-4
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3182238360 [doi]
AB  - Historically, patients presenting with a hemothorax of any cause have been 
      treated with tube thoracostomy. We describe 2 patients with a hemothorax 
      successfully treated with an indwelling tunneled pleural catheter. Our cases may 
      suggest a new treatment modality for selected patients with hemothorax.
